{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Galena and Chicago Union Railroad", "line": "Galena and Chicago Union: Chicago – Freeport", "id": "gcu-chicago-rockford-freeport", "color": "#E3B23C", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 30, "speed_source": "estimated: 1850s-era steam service; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1853, "end": 1864, "headway_min": 480, "note": "Chicago's first railroad, chartered 1836 but delayed by financial trouble until construction began in 1848. Reached Elgin in 1850, Belvidere in 1851, Rockford on Aug 2, 1852, and Freeport (121 miles from Chicago) on Sept 1, 1853. Despite its name, the G&CU itself never reached Galena - the Illinois Central completed that last stretch, Freeport-Galena, in 1854. Frequency estimated, unsourced. START COLLAPSED 1852 -> 1853: the feature is drawn through to Freeport, and Freeport was not reached until 1 Sept 1853. Drawing from the 1852 arrival at Rockford would assert a through line to Freeport a year before one existed.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galena_and_Chicago_Union_Railroad"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-88.841734, 42.2579991], "to": [-89.6212271, 42.2966861], "chord_mi": 39.98, "traced_mi": 43.01, "snap_m": [197, 569], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["Freeport Subdivision (27.65 mi)", "Belvidere Subdivision (14.61 mi)", "(rail) (0.52 mi)", "Rockford Subdivision (0.23 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-87.6244212, 41.8755616], "to": [-88.2810994, 42.03726], "chord_mi": 35.42, "traced_mi": 38.51, "snap_m": [117, 318], "bridged_mi": 0.49, "osm_lines": ["Elgin Subdivision 