0.6647985, 42.5006243]]}}, {"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Chicago and North Western Railway", "line": "Chicago and North Western: Chicago – Freeport (ex-G&CU)", "id": "cnw-chicago-rockford-freeport", "color": "#E3B23C", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 60, "speed_source": "estimated: typical C&NW regional mainline service of the era; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1864, "end": 1875, "headway_min": 180, "note": "The G&CU merged into the Chicago and North Western Railway in 1864. PASSENGER SERVICE CONFIRMED TO 1875 by the Official Guide of that year, which branchline.uk (Illinois route 73) confirms station by station along the whole route. 1875 IS THE LAST CONFIRMED YEAR, NOT A KNOWN END — passenger service on this line certainly ran well into the twentieth century, and this is a large, deliberate understatement. What is established is the other end: by 30 Sept 1951 the line was FREIGHT ONLY, on two independent mechanisms in the Feb 1952 Official Guide — Table 108 \"CHICAGO, ROCKFORD AND FREEPORT\" printed under the heading \"Freight Service only\", and the INDEX OF RAILROAD STATIONS entry \"Rockford, Ill., ... Chic. and N. W., 108+\" carrying the freight-only dagger, while the Milwaukee Road and Illinois Central entries for the same city do not. So passengers ended at an unknown year between 1875 and 1951. This segment previously ran to 1971, which asserted service through at least two decades the Guide shows as freight-only. Do not extend without evidence.", "sources": ["Segment-level: 1875 is the last confirmed passenger year (1875 Official Guide via branchline.uk IL 73); the freight-only status by Sept 1951 is confirmed by the source below. The end is an open floor, not an ending.", "Official Guide of the Railways, Feb 1952 edition (schedules effective 30 Sept 1951), Chicago and North Western System section — local copy research/sources/official_guide_1952.txt", "https://www.branchline.uk/jfpdf/illinoisrrs1.pdf", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galena_and_Chicago_Union_Railroad"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-88.841734, 42.2579991], "to": [-89.6212271, 42.2966861], "chord_mi": 39.98, "traced_mi": 43.01, "snap_m": [197, 569], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["Freeport Subdivision (27.65 mi)", "Belvidere Subdivision (14.61 mi)", "(rail) (0.52 mi)", "Rockford Subdivision (0.23 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-87.6244212, 41.8755616], "to": [-88.2810994, 42.03726], "chord_mi": 35.42, "traced_mi": 38.51, "snap_m": [117, 318], "bridged_mi": 0.49, "osm_lines": ["Elgin Subdivision (29.69 mi)", "C&M Subdivision (2.54 mi)", "UP Geneva Subdivision (2.48 mi)", "Fox River Trail [abandoned] (1.45 mi)", "(?) (0.49 mi)", "University Park Sub District (0.35 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m; 0.49 mi bridged across gaps in OSM"}], "geometry_quality": "Straight-line repair 2026-08-29: 1 ruled segment totalling 40 mi replaced with OpenStreetMap-traced rail geometry (see geometry_repairs for the OSM lines each one followed). Straight-line repair 2026-08-29: 2 ruled segments totalling 75 mi replaced with OpenStreetMap-traced rail geometry (see geometry_repairs for the OSM lines each one followed)."}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-87.6244212, 41.8755616], [-87.6230084, 41.8756488], [-87.6231634, 41.8824475], [-87.6232985, 41.8832972], [-87.6236483, 41.884317], [-87.6236505, 41.8865459], [-87.6267143, 41.8893192], [-87.6271901, 41.888775], [-87.6281927, 41.8885237], [-87.631202, 41.8884784], [-87.6340037, 41.888085], [-87.6340403, 41.8882495], [-87.6339718, 41.88572], [-87.6390046, 41.8856948], [-87.6384938, 41.8857275], [-87.6402459, 41.8855499], [-87.6402145, 41.8850993], [-87.6401318, 41.88491], [-87.6404471, 41.8854193], [-87.6406345, 41.8858872], [-87.6408024, 41.8866508], [-87.6408538, 41.8881658], [-87.6409772, 41.8885806], [